casca-a-classe-dos-arquivos-enviados-standard = The storage class of uploaded files (STANDARD_IA, GLACIER_IR…). Empty: the bucket's.
casca-a-conexao-so-segura-os-tuneis = The connection only holds the tunnels: it doesn't open a shell, and the tab shows what the connection reports.
casca-a-pasta-do-computador-em-que = The folder on this computer where the Files page opens this connection. Empty: the one from Settings > Files, or the home folder.
casca-a-pasta-do-servidor-em-que = The folder on the server where the Files page opens this connection. Empty: the server's home.
casca-a-porta-do-servidor-ssh-e = The server port. SSH and SFTP: 22; FTP: 21 (990 for implicit FTPS); Telnet: 23.
casca-a-senha-do-item-da-credencial = The credential item's password (for S3, the secret key), stored in the vault. Editing saves it to the item (or creates one); clearing the text clears the password. Vault locked: unlock the vault in Tools > Password vault.
casca-a-senha-do-servidor-de-salto = The jump server's password, stored in the vault. Vault locked: unlock the vault in Tools > Password vault.
casca-abre-os-dois-paineis-navegando-juntos = Opens both panes browsing together. Default follows Settings > Files.
casca-abrir-a-conexao-escolhida = Open the selected connection
casca-abrir-arquivos-desta-sessao = Open files for this session
casca-abrir-shell-local = Open local shell
casca-automatica-usa-o-tls-1-3 = Automatic uses TLS 1.3 and falls back to 1.2 on its own if the server doesn't resume the session.
casca-caminho-servidor-bucket-minio-ceph-virtual = Path: server/bucket (MinIO, Ceph). Virtual host: bucket.server (Amazon and most providers).
casca-clique-duas-vezes-numa-conexao-da = Double-click a connection in the tree, or select one and press Enter.
casca-cofre-de-senhas = Password vault
casca-como-a-conexao-e-protegida-ftp = How the connection is protected: FTP over explicit TLS (the default), TLS if available (FTP over explicit TLS, falling back to plain text if the server doesn't offer it), implicit FTPS (port 990) or plain FTP (no encryption). Changing the security changes the port (21 or 990) if it was the default.
casca-como-o-certificado-do-servidor-e = How the server certificate is checked. Don't verify accepts any certificate (a lab MinIO with its own certificate).
casca-como-o-exitonforwardfailure-se-uma-porta = Like ExitOnForwardFailure: if a port doesn't come up, the connection closes instead of opening without the tunnel.
casca-copiar-a-chave-para-o-servidor = Copy the key to the server…
casca-duplicar-a-sessao = Duplicate the session
casca-duplicar-aba = Duplicate tab
