casca-o-arquivo-da-chave-openssh-pem = The key file (OpenSSH, PEM or PuTTY). With no key, the Credential row decides (by default, the password is requested on every connection); ssh-agent keys are also tried.
casca-o-bucket-que-a-conexao-abre = The bucket the connection opens. Empty: the root lists the account's buckets, and each one is a folder.
casca-o-endereco-do-servico-https-s3 = The service address (https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com, http://127.0.0.1:9000…). Changing the region changes the address too, as long as it is the provider's.
casca-o-item-do-cofre-com-o = The vault item with this connection's user and password. Ask when connecting: the password is requested every time.
casca-credencial-da-conexao-descricao = The vault item with this connection's user and password. Inherit: the folder's mode applies (on SSH and SFTP). Ask when connecting: the password is requested every time. SSH agent: signs in with the agent (and the key, if any) without asking; if the server refuses, the tab shows the error. SSH agent, then password: tries the agent and, if the server refuses, asks for the password. On Telnet, the password goes through the "Send the password" step of the commands on connect.
casca-o-agente-foi-recusado = The server accepted neither the SSH agent nor the keys.
casca-o-nome-do-remoto-do-rclone = The name of the rclone remote (what `rclone listremotes` shows, without the colon). Create and edit remotes in Files > rclone remotes.
casca-o-programa-que-o-terminal-desta = The program this local connection's terminal runs, such as wsl.exe, pwsh or docker. Empty: the shell from Settings > Terminal.
casca-o-servidor-apresentou-uma-chave-diferente = The server presented a different key from the one in known_hosts. The connection was refused.
casca-o-token-das-chaves-temporarias-da = The token for temporary AWS keys (STS), stored in the credential item. Empty for regular keys. Vault locked: unlock the vault in Tools > Password vault.
casca-o-usuario-no-servidor-no-s3 = The user on the server (for S3, the Access Key ID). Empty: the credential's user or the local user.
casca-os-argumentos-do-programa-numa-linha = The program's arguments, on one line; quotes group words (for example -d "My Debian" --cd ~).
casca-a-pasta-onde-o-terminal-local-comeca = The folder on this computer where this local connection's terminal starts; accepts ~. Empty: the one from Settings > Terminal, or else the home folder.
