casca-passivo-este-computador-abre-a-conexao = Passive: this computer opens the data connection. Active: the server opens it (needs a port allowed in the firewall). Through the network profile's proxy, only passive mode works.
casca-por-onde-a-conexao-sai-a = How the connection goes out: the network of the group above, direct, or a profile from Tools > Networks. rclone sftp and ftp remotes ignore the profile (rclone has no proxy for them).
casca-por-onde-saem-as-conexoes-do = How the group's connections that didn't choose their own go out: the network of the group above, direct, or a profile from Tools > Networks.
casca-portas-que-o-ssh-encaminha-local = Ports that ssh forwards: local (-L), remote (-R), dynamic SOCKS5 (-D) and the server's Unix socket. They start along with the connection.
